    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offensive core is anchored today by **Drake Baldwin** (71.33) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72), our highest-projected starters. **Drake Baldwin** receives a massive boost from a premium leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Sugano (4.91 xERA), with his xwOBA of .373 signaling sustained production. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against Lopez, J; his score is propelled by a 10% park factor advantage and an 18% bump from the pitcher\u2019s skill profile. **Heliot Ramos** (62.17) also remains a primary start, as he continues to thrive in the heart of the order against Sandoval, maintaining high efficiency despite the platoon dynamic.\n\nWhile **Miguel Vargas** (49.24) was our most compelling bench candidate, he ultimately sits because his projected efficiency is squeezed by a crowded utility slate, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.85) and **Tommy White** (58.45) providing higher baseline floors. We are closely monitoring the defensive outlook for **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.15) and **Jackson Merrill** (46.61); both face suppressed scores due to unfavorable platoon splits and park factors, placing them in the \"marginal\" start category. We are actively protecting game caps by keeping **Miguel Vargas** on the pine, as the marginal gains of his SB upside against Kremer do not currently outweigh the necessity of preserving starts for more favorable weekend matchups.\n\nThe rotation is largely locked in, though the variance in SP matchups remains a point of concern. **Kyle Tucker** (57.59) carries an elevated risk profile today against Anderson, D due to a 14% penalty on the pitcher's skill set, yet he remains in the lineup due to his elite ceiling. With **Andy Pages**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jordan Westburg** unavailable, we are leaning heavily on our depth pieces like **Wade Meckler** (56.54) and **Sam Antonacci** (54.58) to maintain our SB aggression. Owners should watch the wind reports closely, as any shift at the stadium could further dampen the output for **Liam Hicks** (48.40) and **Jackson Merrill**, potentially forcing a late-afternoon swap for **Curtis Mead** or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** if pinch-hit opportunities emerge.",
